{
  "rationale": "Iteration 0 has no race telemetry, so this is a conservative baseline built from the contract. Geometry: five line sensors spread across the centre at 0.02 m spacing (x = -0.02 to +0.02 m) and 0.03 m ahead of the axle, so the tape is always covered by at least one or two sensors on a bend. The 12 mm footprint is wider than the 8 mm option, which gives smoother readings and a larger capture range, while staying well inside the 25 mm tape width. Sensor order runs right to left, with weights -2, -1, 0, +1, +2. Because positive signal steers left, a tape under a left sensor pushes the signal positive and corrects the robot back toward the line. A 0.12 m wheel track and 0.03 m wheel radius give a moderate turn authority, and a 0.8 kg mass keeps yaw inertia low. Controller: base_speed 1.6 (throttle about 80% of full PWM) is a compromise, since the course needs about 1.5 m/s average to finish in 3 s, but higher speed raises the risk of leaving the track on the tighter bends. kp 2.5 gives a turn of about 875 PWM per unit signal, which should hold the line without saturating. ki is kept small (0.1) to avoid integral windup on the bends, and kd 0.05 damps the response without amplifying sensor noise. line_loss 'last_direction' lets the robot recover toward the side it last saw the tape. Expected result: completion on the oval and s-bend, with a moderate rms_error, and the main risk being the slalom at this speed. The next measurements to check are whether the robot completes, its completion_time against the 3 s limit, the max_error on the sharpest bend, and steering_oscillation, which will show whether kp or kd needs changing.",
  "geometry": {
    "sensor_positions": [
      {"x": -0.02, "y": 0.03},
      {"x": -0.01, "y": 0.03},
      {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.03},
      {"x": 0.01, "y": 0.03},
      {"x": 0.02, "y": 0.03}
    ],
    "sensor_size": 0.012,
    "wheel_track": 0.12,
    "wheel_radius": 0.03,
    "body_width": 0.12,
    "body_length": 0.18,
    "mass": 0.8
  },
  "controller": {
    "base_speed": 1.6,
    "kp": 2.5,
    "ki": 0.1,
    "kd": 0.05,
    "sensor_weights": [-2, -1, 0, 1, 2],
    "line_loss": "last_direction"
  },
  "observation_request": {
    "measurements": [
      "completion",
      "progress",
      "completion_time",
      "rms_error",
      "max_error",
      "line_loss_events",
      "steering_oscillation",
      "control_effort"
    ]
  },
  "_presentation": {
    "entity0": {
      "label": "Baseline 5-sensor robot",
      "notes": "Conservative first candidate: five 12 mm sensors with antisymmetric weights, base_speed 1.6, kp 2.5 and light ki/kd. No race data yet, so the values come from the contract's limits and the 1.5 m/s speed requirement."
    }
  }
}
